CPICANN-XRD-App Notice

This repository contains product code, tests, documentation, and small spectrum
fixtures for CPICANN-XRD-App. The application code is distributed under the
license in LICENSE.

The CPICANN model architecture and pretrained checkpoint are external research
artifacts from the upstream CPICANN project. This repository does not include
pretrained weight binaries, tokens, or private download credentials.

The XDecomposer integration added for the v0.2.0 release candidate includes
schemas, manifests, optional entry points, an isolated worker, orchestration,
job APIs, validation tooling, and a minimal vendored copy of MIT-licensed
upstream XDecomposer model source used by the worker. This repository does not
include XDecomposer checkpoints, MAE-pretraining checkpoints, reference banks,
dataset caches, tokens, or private download credentials.

The committed catalog files are used to map CPICANN class indices to phase
metadata for reproducible local inference. Redistribution of the upstream model
weights must be handled separately by users according to the upstream source and
their institutional policy.

Prediction confidence values are model ranking scores after optional filtering.
They are not quantitative phase fractions or material composition estimates.

XDecomposer component weights and CPICANN conditional confidence values are
experimental outputs until scientific validation is signed for a defined data
domain.
